@baseUrl = http://localhost:4002
@adminToken = replace-with-admin-token

### Public published list
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/faqs?page=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

### Public detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/faqs/what-are-your-business-hours
Accept: application/json

### Drafts and authoring require an administrator bearer token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/faqs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "example-draft",
  "question": "What is this example?",
  "answer": "This is an example answer with enough content for the request.",
  "category": "Getting started",
  "seoDescription": "A concise answer describing this example FAQ entry.",
  "isDraft": true
}

### Update an entry without changing its stable key
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/faqs/example-draft
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "What is this updated example?",
  "answer": "This is an updated example answer with enough content for the request.",
  "category": "Getting started",
  "seoDescription": "An updated FAQ description with enough content for the request.",
  "isDraft": true
}

### Delete an entry
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/faqs/example-draft
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Missing detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/faqs/does-not-exist
Accept: application/json

### 401 without an administrator token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/faqs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "unauthorised-example",
  "question": "Can an unauthorised caller write?",
  "answer": "This request should be rejected before a FAQ row is written.",
  "category": "Testing",
  "seoDescription": "An unauthorised FAQ request must not be accepted."
}

### Match a keyword against one field of the caller's shape; leave field out to match every text field
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/faqs?field=category&keyword=news

### A field the caller's shape does not carry (isDraft for an anonymous reader): 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/faqs?field=isDraft&keyword=true
